    "long_instructions": "# Polishing the App\r\n\r\n1. **Identify Edge Cases:** Prompt the AI to find weaknesses in your code and design. You might ask:\r\n   - *What are potential edge cases for my filtering system?*\r\n   - *How do I handle situations where the data is missing a value?*\r\n   - *What happens if filters return no results or combine in confusing ways?*\r\n\r\n2. **Handle Errors and Improve Clarity:** Update your JavaScript with conditional logic (`if/else`) to fix at least two issues.\r\n   - **Note:** Common fixes include converting text to `toLowerCase()` before comparing, checking if a value exists (`!== undefined`) before displaying it, or showing a clear “No results found” message.\r\n\r\n3. **Revise for Fairness and Transparency:** Adjust any filters, labels, thresholds, or messages that could confuse users or hide important items.\r\n\r\n4. **Final Polish:** Clean up your layout, labels, and comments. Add comments to explain your code sections, such as `// Filter Logic` or `// Event Listeners`. Run your app one last time to ensure the Undo button, Reset button, filters, sorting, labels, and result count all work together smoothly.",
